# Copy to .env.local and fill in what you need. Every variable is optional.

# Postgres database for shared documents (the Share button). Leave unset to
# hide sharing; everything else works without it. The table is created on
# first use. Local example, after:
#   docker run -d -p 5432:5432 -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=pg postgres
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:pg@localhost:5432/postgres

# Public origin for canonical links, the sitemap, robots.txt and Open Graph
# images. Defaults to https://andiko.app; set it when self-hosting elsewhere. The
# terms (/terms) name the site's address only when this is set.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://notes.example.com

# Who runs this instance, shown in its privacy policy (/privacy) and terms (/terms).
# Those pages and the links to them are only published when the name, email and
# region are set; the Report link on shared documents needs only the email. Baked in
# at build time, like NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL. Both pages describe sharing, so set these
# with DATABASE_URL.
# When a company runs it, give its full legal name, legal form included, and its
# registered office and companies register entry, so both pages show the company as
# the one you deal with.
# The regions say where shared documents are stored (the database) and processed (the
# server). They only describe the deployment, so keep them in step with your Neon project
# and your Vercel Functions region. The server region is optional; the policy leaves it
# out when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OPERATOR_NAME=Example Ltd
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OPERATOR_ADDRESS=KG 7 Ave, Kigali, Rwanda
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OPERATOR_REGISTRATION=Registered in Rwanda, company code 123456789
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=privacy@example.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DATABASE_REGION=EU (Frankfurt)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_REGION=EU (Frankfurt)

# Chrome binary for PDF export, e.g. in Docker. Local development uses the
# Chrome downloaded by puppeteer, and Vercel/AWS Lambda use @sparticuz/chromium.
# CHROME_EXECUTABLE_PATH=/usr/bin/chromium
